# Line endings for the client-facing launchers.
#
# ⚠️ The `.cmd` files are double-clicked on a Windows machine, and until F4.5
# they were stored and checked out LF-only with nothing asserting otherwise —
# the eol of a client-facing artifact was whatever the packaging step happened
# to produce. cmd.exe's handling of LF-only batch files is version-dependent and
# the known failures are exactly around labels and `goto`, which is the
# construct start.cmd now leans on harder after F4.5 removed its `call`
# subroutine. This eliminates the risk by construction rather than by hoping.
#
# ⚠️ NOT VERIFIED on a real Windows machine — Wine's cmd is indifferent to line
# endings, so the harness cannot see this either way. It is a safe change made
# because it is free, not because a test caught it. F5.9 is what can confirm it.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# The shell twin must stay LF; CRLF breaks a shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf
